# CineLog V2 — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# For production, set these in the Vercel dashboard:
#   Settings → Environment Variables
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY MODEL
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All variables use the `VITE_` prefix, which Vite exposes to the
# client-side bundle. This is intentional — these are all PUBLIC,
# read-only keys designed by their providers to be shipped to browsers:
#
#   • Supabase ANON key — safe to expose. RLS policies enforce row-level
#     security; the anon key cannot bypass them. The Supabase SERVICE
#     ROLE key is NEVER used in the application runtime and must NEVER
#     be added here. It is reserved for trusted admin scripts (DB
#     migrations) and Supabase Edge Functions only.
#
#   • TMDB API key — TMDB's v3 API key is a read-only key meant for
#     client-side use. Rate limits apply per-key.
#
#   • OMDb API key — free, read-only, rate-limited. Safe to expose.
#
#   If you need a server-side secret (e.g. for webhooks, service-role
#   operations, or third-party APIs that require a private key), do NOT
#   use the `VITE_` prefix — use a plain name (e.g. `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`)
#   so Vite keeps it server-only.
#
#   • SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — used ONLY by server API routes
#     (/api/tmdb-cache) to read/write the tmdb_cache table. NEVER exposed
#     to the browser (no VITE_ prefix).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase (https://app.supabase.com → Your Project → Settings → API)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Supabase Service Role Key — SERVER-ONLY, never expose to the browser!
# Used by /api/tmdb-cache route to read/write the tmdb_cache table.
# Find it at: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → service_role key (secret)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# TMDB API (https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api → API Key)
VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=

# OMDb API (https://www.omdbapi.com/apikey.aspx)
VITE_OMDB_API_KEY=
